Time: O(nlogn)
Space: O(1)
space O(n) worst case	Python's sorting can use auxiliary memory; the sliding window itself uses O(1)

class Solution:
    def maximumBeauty(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:
        nums.sort()
        l = 0
        max_len = 0
        for r in range(len(nums)):
            while nums[r] - nums[l] > 2*k:
                l += 1
            max_len = max(max_len, r-l+1)
        return max_len

We want the maximum number of ranges that share at least one common value
